  "current_implementation_evidence": [
    "THE INDEX IS NOT ALLOWED TO ANSWER ITS OWN QUESTION. An earlier derivation resolved 194 members to the successor baseline candidate, which enumerates all 990 subject ids by construction. The disposition ledger and its producer-evidence input are therefore added to the binding layer's self-enumeration exclusions, so producing this ledger CANNOT change one member's producer attribution. Measured after the change: the binding layer still reports 194 unattributed producers, unchanged, and check-canonical-estate still emits its 16 withheld-owner SKIPs.",
    "THE DERIVATION IS THE GIT HISTORY OF THE PRODUCER. A single pass over every unique historical text blob outside docs/evidence asks, for each member, whether any tracked blob literally names it — by exact path, by basename, or by the schemaVersion the member's own bytes declare. 185 of the 194 are named by at least one; every producer so found is absent from the bound tree and git names the commit that removed it. The largest single family is not a guess: 154 members declare one schemaVersion, and exactly ONE historical blob in the whole repository emits that schema.",
    "A REBIND IS NOT A RETIREMENT, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS DERIVED. The producer set was renamed once and retired later. `git show -M` is asked whether the removing commit recorded the path as a rename source, so `rename_rebind` and `retirement` are distinguishable facts rather than a reading of a commit subject.",
    "THE NUMBER FELL BY DERIVATION AND THE REMAINDER WAS DECIDED, NOT DERIVED. 194 unattributed members became 9 by derivation. The 9 are members for which NO tracked blob anywhere in this repository's history names them by any of the three axes; the only remaining routes to an owner would be the directory they sit in or the enumeration that lists them, and both stay refused by name. On 2026-07-29 the OWNER decided those 9 individually, at their exact paths and digests, under owner-ruling://2026-07-29/overlay-attribution-and-manifest-succession. The derivation did not improve; a person chose. The ledger records that on every one of the 9 as decision_source explicit_owner_ruling, no family rule enumerates them, and the bar refuses the mislabel in both directions.",
    "RETIREMENT NO LONGER CONTRADICTS THE FREEZE. The governing rule said retirement required a tombstone appended to the frozen manifest's retired_members, which directed an edit into frozen subject frz-0002 — so the append rule and the freeze rule could not both be obeyed, while two identities sat tombstoned in this ledger with nothing carrying them. The model is now: retirement is recorded in the disposition/tombstone ledger and carried into the next immutable manifest version; a frozen manifest is never edited. The candidate successor carries all 220 identities at v1's own digests, 218 active and 2 retired, binds v1 by both digests, and remains unadmitted.",
    "AN EXCEPTION THE RULE REFUSED IS EXPOSED, NOT ABSORBED. The retirement family enumerates superseded drafts whose final counterpart is itself a bound member; one of the three candidates is cited twice by retained evidence, so it is refused by the rule, named individually with the reason, and falls through to a successor assignment instead."
